# FIX SLOW RESPONSE - OPTIMISTIC UPDATES

Problem: App slow when adding/deleting tasks and events
Solution: Update UI immediately, sync database in background

---

## CONCEPT

### Current (SLOW):
```
1. Database operation (500ms)
2. Refetch all data (500ms)  
3. UI updates (1000ms total) ❌
```

### New (FAST):
```
1. Update UI immediately (10ms) ✅
2. Database operation in background
```

---

## FIX: ALL THREE HOOKS

Apply this pattern to useTasks.ts, useShoppingItems.ts, and useEvents.ts:

### CREATE
```typescript
const createTask = async (taskData) => {
  const { data, error } = await supabase
    .from('tasks')
    .insert(taskData)
    .select()
    .single();

  if (error) return { data: null, error: error.message };

  setTasks(prev => [data, ...prev]); // Immediate update
  return { data, error: null };
};
```

### UPDATE
```typescript
const updateTask = async (taskId, updates) => {
  // Update UI first
  setTasks(prev => prev.map(t => 
    t.id === taskId ? { ...t, ...updates } : t
  ));

  // Then database
  const { data, error } = await supabase
    .from('tasks')
    .update(updates)
    .eq('id', taskId)
    .select()
    .single();

  if (error) {
    await loadTasks(); // Revert on error
    return { data: null, error: error.message };
  }

  return { data, error: null };
};
```

### DELETE
```typescript
const deleteTask = async (taskId) => {
  // Remove from UI first
  setTasks(prev => prev.filter(t => t.id !== taskId));

  // Then database
  const { error } = await supabase
    .from('tasks')
    .delete()
    .eq('id', taskId);

  if (error) {
    await loadTasks(); // Revert on error
    return { error: error.message };
  }

  return { error: null };
};
```

### COMPLETE/TOGGLE
```typescript
const completeTask = async (taskId) => {
  // Mark complete in UI first
  setTasks(prev => prev.map(t => 
    t.id === taskId ? { ...t, completed: true } : t
  ));

  // Then database
  await supabase
    .from('tasks')
    .update({ completed: true })
    .eq('id', taskId);
};
```

---

## APPLY TO ALL HOOKS

### hooks/useTasks.ts
- createTask → Add to state immediately
- updateTask → Update state first
- deleteTask → Remove from state first
- completeTask → Toggle state first

### hooks/useShoppingItems.ts
- addItem → Add to state immediately
- updateItem → Update state first
- deleteItem → Remove from state first
- markPurchased → Toggle state first

### hooks/useEvents.ts
- createEvent → Add to state immediately
- updateEvent → Update state first
- deleteEvent → Remove from state first

---

## REMOVE REFETCHES

Delete these lines from mutations:
```typescript
await loadTasks();    // DELETE
await loadItems();    // DELETE
await loadEvents();   // DELETE
```

Only keep refetch in error handlers to revert failed operations.

---

## RESULT

- ✅ Instant UI updates
- ✅ Snappy, responsive feel
- ✅ Database syncs in background
- ✅ Errors handled gracefully
- ✅ Realtime still works

Test:
- [ ] Create task → Instant
- [ ] Delete task → Instant
- [ ] Create event → Instant
- [ ] Feels fast and smooth

DONE!

